error[Z0401]: tabulate takes one or two variables, not 3
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:12
  |
2 | f.tabulate([a, b, c])
  |            ^^^^^^^^^ the variables to tabulate
  |
  = help: write one variable, `tabulate(industry)`, or two in a list, `tabulate([industry, female])`

error[Z0401]: `percent: row` and `percent: col` need two variables; one variable's table always shows the percentage of all rows
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:24
  |
2 | f.tabulate(a, percent: row)
  |                        ^^^ row or column percentages of a one-way table
  |
  = help: give two variables, `tabulate([industry, female], percent: row)`, or leave `percent:` out

error[Z0401]: `percent: row` and `percent: col` need two variables; one variable's table always shows the percentage of all rows
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:24
  |
2 | f.tabulate(a, percent: col)
  |                        ^^^ row or column percentages of a one-way table
  |
  = help: give two variables, `tabulate([industry, female], percent: row)`, or leave `percent:` out

error[Z0402]: `cell` is not one of the allowed words
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:24
  |
2 | f.tabulate(a, percent: cell)
  |                        ^^^^ expected one of row, col, total

